WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.525
AI coding assistants can draft
these scripts in seconds.

2
00:00:03.525 --> 00:00:06.580
The catch is that they can
draft mistakes just as fast,

3
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:08.663
and they sound confident either way.

4
00:00:08.663 --> 00:00:10.137
So the rules are simple.

5
00:00:10.137 --> 00:00:14.255
First, use only tools the agency
has approved under its AI policy,

6
00:00:14.255 --> 00:00:20.549
which the Office of Management and Budget's
memo M-25-21 asks every agency to have.

7
00:00:20.549 --> 00:00:23.424
Second, never put real data, passwords,

8
00:00:23.424 --> 00:00:27.688
or secrets into a prompt; we
use made-up examples instead.

9
00:00:27.688 --> 00:00:31.863
Third, a named person reads
every line before it's accepted.

10
00:00:31.863 --> 00:00:37.338
NIST, the National Institute of Standards
and Technology, takes the same position:

11
00:00:37.338 --> 00:00:41.363
AI-written code is reviewed
exactly like code a person wrote.

12
00:00:41.363 --> 00:00:45.290
And because assistants sometimes
invent functions that don't exist,

13
00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:49.287
every platform call gets checked
against the vendor's documentation.

14
00:00:49.287 --> 00:00:52.940
"The AI wrote it" is never
a reason to accept a line.
